cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "linear-baseline: honest linear baselines for cis-regulatory sequence-to-function prediction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tri-Omics Transformer project"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/akalh233-bot/linear-baseline"
keywords:
  - regulatory genomics
  - TF binding
  - CRE-gene linkage
  - baseline
  - logistic regression
abstract: >-
  A minimal, reproducible logistic-regression baseline for TF-CRE and CRE-gene
  prediction with locus-aware splits, average-precision evaluation and
  cluster-level bootstrap confidence intervals. Includes a real-data full-bio
  arm on the EPCrisprBenchmark K562 CRE->gene task (leave-one-chromosome-out,
  AP 0.6715, 0.6507 without measured chromatin marks).
